  "description": "Realised gains on the portfolio's AVCO basis (not the FIFO of the tax view): one row per sale, in trade order (instant, then BUY before SELL, then externalId, then id), amounts in euros with fees inside both the cost and the proceeds. A swap is valued at the greater of its two legs, less its fee. Units received in kind (funding IN_KIND) enter the average at their value. price is gross over quantity; returnPct is realised over cost to six places, null on a zero cost; holdingDays is the sale instant minus the quantity-weighted acquisition instant of what was held, in days rounded half up, null when nothing was held. Shared with the mobile client: both implementations must reproduce every case. Events are LedgerEvents; an absent fxSource is IDENTITY and an absent funding is CASH. expect is written by running the TypeScript core; byHand.figures, where a case has it, are worked out by hand, its arithmetic says how, and each key is a dotted path into expect.",
